The directory `packages/leads-core/` is maintained upstream in that
repository and is mirrored here with `git subtree`. Changes to it should
be made upstream and pulled in, so the two products do not diverge:

    npm run core:pull

The upstream branch is `leads-core-dist`, which carries the package
alone. It is produced from the anomalia repository with:

    git subtree split --prefix=packages/leads-core -b leads-core-dist
    git push origin leads-core-dist

That split has to be re-run upstream whenever the package changes: a
plain branch does not follow a subdirectory on its own.
